webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9403042Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9411396Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9496733Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9506310Z ^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9506990Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9508159Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9508640Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9508945Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9509599Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9509994Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9510259Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9510784Z    if you are ready to continue.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9511011Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9511508Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9512181Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9512614Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9512914Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9513063Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9513214Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9513424Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9513659Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9513970Z    can use Nix.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9514096Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9514394Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9514583Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9515311Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9515921Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9525313Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9525648Z I will:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9525901Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9526100Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9526494Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9526857Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9527208Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9527463Z  - install Nix in /nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9527717Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9528067Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9528389Z    /root
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9705835Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9706575Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9715861Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9716386Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9716751Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9717856Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9718299Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9733250Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9733782Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9742545Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9743191Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9743585Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9743799Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9744001Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9744407Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9744564Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9744901Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9745076Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9745172Z If you would like to
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9745400Z see the output, try like this:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:31:03.9745546Z 
